# Build context exclusions.
#
# `docker_data/` is the single reason this file has to exist: it is a live
# bind-mount target held open by the running containers, so including it makes
# the build fail outright with "open docker_data: Access is denied" on Windows
# before a single layer is written. Everything else here is size and secrecy.

# Live database state — locked while containers run, and never needed in an image
docker_data/
qdrant_*db/
qdrant_*db_*/

# Secrets — the image must receive keys via the environment, never baked in
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local virtualenvs — the image installs its own dependencies
.venv/
venv/

# VCS, editor and agent-tooling state
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
.remember/

# Python caches and test artifacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Model / embedding caches — multi-GB, re-downloaded inside the image
.cache/
models/

# Logs and scratch
*.log
**/*.log
logs/
scratchpad/

# Deal documents are mounted at runtime via the ./data volume, not copied in
data/

# Private notes and job-application material — never belong in a pushed image
ppp.md
PROJECT_KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md
questions_mock.md
ai_engineer_interview_guide.md
auric*

# Frontend — deployed separately to Vercel, and never imported by the API. Its
# node_modules alone is several hundred MB of build context the backend image
# would copy and never open. (node_modules is listed on its own as well, so it
# stays out even if web/ is ever re-included for a frontend image.)
web/
web/node_modules/

*.local.md
